Five working diagrams of how this project fits together, straight from the project's own planning docs. 

***Colors have been attempted to recycle the CityLink pallete oWo***

FYI, three are posted unedited and these are subject to change; the release provers and decion matrices have been simplified public versions stand in for those instead.  If you want the full cronch ask for access to the the meta repo in GFTB gh. 


**How tool moves** 

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/inventory-custody-flow.svg" alt="Inventory custody flow: scan a tool, check its availability and condition, finalize a loan, then scan it back in, inspect it, and route it to available or quarantine." />

**How a change gets safely onto the site.** Reviewed, built, checked twice, deployed  :-)

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/release-proof-flow-public.svg" alt="Release proof flow: reviewed by another person, built into a release, checked twice (automated tests, then a human check), deployed to the site, confirmed actually serving and not just deployed, then recorded as done; if something's wrong, rolled back to the last working version instead." />


Descision flow:

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/launch-authority-flow-public.svg" alt="Launch authority flow: members' personal facts stay private; applications to join go to keyholders, who decide on admission; money and payments are handled separately from membership decisions; releases of the site get the operator's sign-off." />
